StockRegistry executable-depth gate
├── given no configuration, missing pool state, or zero active liquidity
│   └── reject enabling even when the minimum is zero and balances are donated
├── given a canonical venue quote
│   ├── when CALL is required by the quoter
│   │   └── support reverting swap simulation without STATICCALL
│   ├── when a quote fails, runs out of gas, is malformed, zero, or overflows
│   │   └── report zero and fail the gate without reverting the report
│   ├── when the feed is unusable, stale, future dated, or uninitialized
│   │   └── fail closed
│   ├── when execution lies outside either Chainlink deviation bound
│   │   └── fail closed
│   └── when a finite probe executes within the bound
│       ├── report the configured input USD notional without extrapolation
│       ├── accept exactly the configured minimum threshold
│       └── quote once per report entry
├── given donation of either token on either venue
│   ├── increase informational balances and TVL
│   └── preserve active liquidity, executable depth, and failing enablement
└── given governance configuration
    ├── reject unauthorized callers, wrong factories, and unsafe bounds
    ├── disable on probe configuration changes
    └── invalidate configuration on venue changes
